# wheel-stacked (M9): in the stacked layout (800 x 900: the panel above the plane, the page
# scrolling) the wheel scrolls the page over the panel and zooms the plane over the plane, the page
# staying (useZoom.ts's listener is not passive and prevents the scroll). The plane is (16, 824.5,
# 768 x 480) in the page, which scrolls 421 px (the reference's DOM); the wheel over the panel's left
# padding (x 25, no row under it) takes it to its foot, the plane then at (16, 403.5); D17's zoom is
# 40 px a unit there (80 %), the origin at (384, 240) in the plane. A notch of −100 px at (584, 544),
# 200 px right of the plane's centre and 99.5 up, zooms about it: 40 · exp(0.15) = 46.47 px a unit.
# (A pointer at a half px is no use here: WebKit hands a page whole-px clientX and clientY.)
# Chromium hands the wheel over at half its delta, on the reference too.
size 800 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 25 400
wheel 0 1000
wait 16
shot scrolled
move 584 544
wait 500
wheel 0 -100
wait 16
shot zoomed
